{"id": "sdqa0121", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1644703104, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "9d39a2003e15ffbac1b46fe5b0a53c242ef024ed6b8b1e37a92e22d426213d95", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "What is exponentiation?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0121.wav", "input_sha256": "02f0d7d269537e7a11afc2d6427061eac2df1a41203dce537a60fdbb108ebd18", "input_samples": 76453, "input_s": 4.778, "n_real_chunks": 5, "score": 0.1504, "act": 0.9977, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Exponentiation is a mathematical operation that means raising a number to a power. For example: \\[ 2^3 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 8 \\] Here: 2 is the base , 3 is the exponent or power , \\(2^3\\) means “multiply 2 by itself 3 times” So, in general: \\[ a^n \\] means multiplying \\(a\\) by itself \\(n\\) times, when \\(n\\) is a positive whole number.", "expert_answer": "**Exponentiation** is a mathematical operation that means **raising a number to a power**.\n\nFor example:\n\n\\[\n2^3 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 8\n\\]\n\nHere:\n\n- **2** is the **base**\n- **3** is the **exponent** or **power**\n- \\(2^3\\) means “multiply 2 by itself 3 times”\n\nSo, in general:\n\n\\[\na^n\n\\]\n\nmeans multiplying \\(a\\) by itself \\(n\\) times, when \\(n\\) is a positive whole number.", "transcript": "What is exponentiation?\n", "asr_s": 0.48, "expert_s": 5.17, "expert_input_samples": 76453, "expert_input_s": 4.778, "expert_input_sha256": "02f0d7d269537e7a11afc2d6427061eac2df1a41203dce537a60fdbb108ebd18", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 4.398, "relay_synth_ms": 57355, "onset_chunk": 5, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 175, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 175, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa