{"id": "sdqa0000", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 653989283, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "9d39a2003e15ffbac1b46fe5b0a53c242ef024ed6b8b1e37a92e22d426213d95", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 0, "query": "When was quantum field theory developed?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0000.wav", "input_sha256": "4f5b478df82f6544dbb54ce0ef7c3355805bd5aec1ba29f897fbc809fd72f80e", "input_samples": 98640, "input_s": 6.165, "n_real_chunks": 7, "score": 0.4719, "act": 0.9993, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Quantum field theory was developed mainly in the late 1920s and 1930s. Key milestones: 1927: Paul Dirac formulated the first quantum theory of the electromagnetic field. , Late 1920s–1930s: Heisenberg, Pauli, Fermi, and others developed early QFT. , 1940s: Modern renormalized QFT was developed by Tomonaga, Schwinger, Feynman, and Dyson.", "expert_answer": "Quantum field theory was developed mainly in the **late 1920s and 1930s**.\n\nKey milestones:\n- **1927:** Paul Dirac formulated the first quantum theory of the electromagnetic field.\n- **Late 1920s–1930s:** Heisenberg, Pauli, Fermi, and others developed early QFT.\n- **1940s:** Modern renormalized QFT was developed by Tomonaga, Schwinger, Feynman, and Dyson.", "transcript": "When was quantum field theory developed?\n", "asr_s": 3.21, "expert_s": 3.03, "expert_input_samples": 98640, "expert_input_s": 6.165, "expert_input_sha256": "4f5b478df82f6544dbb54ce0ef7c3355805bd5aec1ba29f897fbc809fd72f80e", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 0.423, "relay_synth_ms": 15435, "onset_chunk": 6, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 3, "feed_lag_max_ms": 2959, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 8604, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0000_always_rela